muros (0.9.90) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A firewall reload replaced the entire nftables ruleset, which also took
    away the tables other parts of the system own. The captive portal keeps
    its authenticated clients and their traffic counters in one of them, so
    every reload disconnected the users of a portal zone and reset the volume
    they had consumed, which meant a data quota was never reached on a machine
    that reloads its firewall. The generated ruleset now replaces its own
    table and nothing else, in the same single transaction.

