muros (0.9.89) trixie; urgency=medium

  * NAT reflection, the last NAT feature with nothing behind it. A host on an
    inside network that asks for the published address now gets the same
    translation as one coming from outside, with the return path translated so
    the answer comes back through the firewall. It follows the per-rule
    setting and the two system settings, for port forwards and for 1:1
    mappings.
  * A rule naming several interfaces resolved to none of them, which left it
    matching every interface instead of the two it was bound to.
  * An IPv6 interface network was written as the interface address with its
    prefix length, naming one host where the subnet was meant.

