muros (0.9.87) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Aliases whose content is not a list of addresses (GeoIP countries, URL
    tables, host names, MAC addresses, autonomous system numbers, nested
    groups) were emptied by every firewall reload. pf kept the contents of its
    tables across a reload, nftables starts from a flushed ruleset, so the
    rules using those aliases matched nothing until the updater ran again, up
    to a minute later. The generated ruleset now carries the resolved
    addresses itself, so an alias is armed the moment the ruleset is loaded.
  * The rule check reports an alias that ends up with no address at all,
    instead of leaving a rule loaded that can never match.

