muros (0.9.78) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The changelog tab of the firmware page shows something. It used to download
    a tarball of pre-rendered changelogs from the OPNsense mirrors, the port
    replaced that with an empty stub, and an operator had no way to see what an
    update contained. A Debian package carries its own changelog, so the history
    up to the running version is already on the box and apt can fetch the one of
    a version not installed yet: both are turned into the per version text, HTML
    and index the page reads. The repository publishes the changelog of every
    package alongside it and the box ships the apt configuration that points
    there, so a pending update can be read before it is applied.
  * The sqlite3 repair path called a FreeBSD path that does not exist here, so a
    corrupted database was dumped into an empty file and reimported from it. The
    command is looked up now, and the repair is skipped when it is not
    installed.
  * Removed the inert FreeBSD ifconfig parser left next to the iproute2 one.

