muros (0.9.76) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Source NAT rules are applied again. The Source NAT page writes into the
    model tree while the older Outbound page keeps writing the legacy section,
    and the ruleset builder only read the legacy one: a rule created on the
    current page was accepted, listed and counted in the GUI, and the traffic
    still left the box with whatever source address the automatic masquerade
    picked. Such a rule is rendered now, one line per transport protocol it
    covers. An interface or interface address target becomes a masquerade, so a
    dynamic uplink keeps working across an address change, a fixed address
    becomes an snat and a prefix an snat to the pool it spans. A target port is
    only emitted with a known transport protocol, static-port leaves the target
    without one and lets connection tracking preserve the original port, and
    the No-NAT rules are placed ahead of every translating rule. A target that
    resolves to an alias is still skipped, nftables cannot translate to a set.

