muros (0.9.60) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Scripts: the Python and PHP shebangs point at the Debian interpreters.
    Ninety scripts, configd and configd_ctl among them, still started with
    #!/usr/local/bin/python3, a path nothing creates, so every one of them failed
    with a missing interpreter as soon as configd, a syshook or a cron job
    executed it directly.
  * System: lighttpd (web GUI and captive portal), syslog-ng and syslog-ng-ctl,
    dnsmasq and rrdtool are started from their Debian paths instead of the
    FreeBSD prefix, which nothing symlinks. The health graphs, the logging
    backend and the GUI restart all failed with a missing binary. syslog-ng-core
    and rrdtool are now dependencies, dnsmasq a recommendation.
  * IPv6 prefix delegation: an interface set to track6 is rendered with
    DHCPPrefixDelegation pointing at its upstream interface and the configured
    prefix id as subnet id, so a LAN tracking a DHCPv6 WAN finally receives a
    prefix. The apply only sent a HUP to a dhcp6c that does not exist.
  * Router advertisements: radvd is started from /usr/sbin and its configuration
    digest is computed with sha256sum, not the FreeBSD sha256(1). Advertisements
    were never sent at all, and the digest mismatch respawned the daemon on
    every configure. radvd is now a dependency.
  * Firmware: the upgrade sanity hook checks dpkg and apt-get instead of
    pkg-static, verifies the core package is installed and refuses to run on a
    half configured dpkg database. The crash reporter lists the installed
    plugins with dpkg.
  * Unbound: the configuration generator no longer builds the FreeBSD jail
    layout under /var/unbound, including a Python runtime directory derived from
    a path that does not exist here. Unbound runs without a chroot on this
    platform.

